Seed appearance and experimental settings from the runtime

A freshly provisioned workspace could not declare how its Orca looks or which
features are on: every browser opening the tile started at stock defaults, and
the same toggles got re-clicked after every workspace create.

The web client keeps settings in localStorage, and of the 184 top-level
`GlobalSettings` keys on `v1.4.156` it pulls exactly five from the runtime -
`theme` and the `experimental*` flags are not among them, so writing
`orca-data.json` on the workspace changed nothing. A shared allowlist of
appearance and capability keys is now returned by `settings.get` and adopted
exactly once, on a browser's first visit, when localStorage holds no settings
blob; nothing is written back and nothing is re-imposed later, so these are
defaults rather than policy. Per-device ergonomics and credentials are excluded.
A load that never reached the store does not spend the first visit, so a browser
whose first open happened offline still seeds on the next one.

To test, set a seeded key in the workspace's `orca-data.json` and open the tile
in a browser with no Orca localStorage; then change it in the UI and reload to
confirm the workspace does not override the user. Covered by
`runtime-seeded-settings.test.ts` for the key picker and
`web-preload-settings-seeding.test.ts` for the load path.

